Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Stand in for Workspace, Package, Target and
 RustcTargetData

The lock file encoder walks workspace members and their path dependencies
and reads `[patch]` and `[replace]`; the feature resolver asks which
members to resolve for, whether a package's library is a proc-macro, and
whether a dependency's platform applies to a compile kind. Cargo answers
from manifests on disk and from `rustc --print cfg`. These types have the
methods the moved code calls, over what the embedding application supplies.
`RecursivePathSource`, which Cargo uses to suggest packages near a missing
path dependency, finds nothing.
